#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# fourier_sequence_transform

#% text
# `fourier_sequence_transform(f, k, w)` gives the discrete-time Fourier transform of the sequence f(k): the sum of `f(k) exp(-im k w)` over all integers k.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# By linearity: `discrete_delta(k - k0)` gives `exp(-im k0 w)`; a one-sided term `g(k) unit_step(k - k0)` or `g(k) unit_step(k1 - k)` is a Z transform at `z = exp(im w)` or `exp(-im w)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
fourier_sequence_transform((1/2)^k*unit_step(k), k, w)
#% output
#= 2*exp(im*w)/(-1 + 2*exp(im*w))

#% cell
fourier_sequence_transform(discrete_delta(k - k0), k, w)
#% output
#= exp(-im*k0*w)

#% cell
fourier_sequence_transform(unit_step(k)/factorial(k), k, w)
#% output
#= exp(exp(-im*w))

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `z_transform`, `fourier_transform`
